Code following a comment's `;` on the same line is executable and easy
to misread as part of the comment: comment_text_after_terminator,
same-line continuation path, warning (diag.comment_text_after_terminator
first Flags fence).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE ResetFlags;
	:DECLARE bDirty, bLocked;
	/* clear both flags; bDirty := .F.;
	bLocked := .F.;
	:RETURN bLocked;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE ResetFlags;
	:DECLARE bDirty, bLocked;
	/* clear both flags;
	bDirty := .F.;
	bLocked := .F.;
	:RETURN bLocked;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
3:2-3:22 warning comment_text_after_terminator: Comment terminated early by semicolon. Text after the ';' becomes executable code and may be unintentionally hidden
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
3:2-3:22 warning comment_text_after_terminator: Comment terminated early by semicolon. Text after the ';' becomes executable code and may be unintentionally hidden
